# /learn: project learnings

**Hard gate:** manage learnings only. Make no code changes, even when a learning names a fix.

`~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-learnings-search` reads this project's learnings (latest entry per key+type);
`~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-learnings-log` appends one. Both take `--help`. Pick the mode from the request:

| Request | Run | Then |
|---|---|---|
| show (default) | `gstack-learnings-search --limit 20` | group by type; if empty, say none are recorded yet and that /review, /ship, /investigate and other skills record them as they work |
| search | `gstack-learnings-search --query "<words>" --limit 20` | show the matches |
| other projects | add `--cross-project` | only user-stated learnings from other projects appear |
| stats | `gstack-learnings-search --stats` | show the counts as a table |
| export | `gstack-learnings-search --limit 50` | a `## Project Learnings` section, `### <Type>s` per type, lines `- **key**: insight (confidence: N/10)`; show it, and write it into CLAUDE.md or a file only if the user asks |
| add | `gstack-learnings-log '<json>'` | ask only for what is missing: type, kebab-case key, one-sentence insight, confidence 1-10, files; `"source":"user-stated"` |
| prune | `gstack-learnings-search --limit 100` | see Prune |

## Prune

Flag each learning that is:
- **STALE**: a path in its `files` no longer exists in the repo.
- **CONFLICT**: the same key appears under two types with opposing insights (within one type the latest entry already wins).

For each flagged entry, unless the user already approved the action, ask: remove, keep, or update.
- Remove: delete its lines (that key and type) from `$GSTACK_STATE_ROOT/projects/$SLUG/learnings.jsonl`, where
  `SLUG=$(~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-slug --get SLUG)` and
  `GSTACK_STATE_ROOT=$(~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-paths --get GSTACK_STATE_ROOT)`. Leave every other line as it is.
- Update: log a corrected entry with the same key and type; the latest one wins.
